Relevant tables and columns for monthly balance reporting

customer_transactions  
• customer_id: identifies each customer – used for grouping and joining  
• txn_date: the calendar date of the movement – used for generating year‑month buckets and for ordering transactions chronologically  
• txn_type: tells us whether the movement adds to, or subtracts from, the balance (e.g. deposit = +, withdrawal = –). We must inspect values to confirm sign logic  
• txn_amount: size of the movement – will be signed (+/–) and aggregated to monthly change figures  

Possible filtering / transformation conditions  
• strftime('%Y‑%m', txn_date) AS month_year  → collapses any date to its calendar month  
• CASE txn_type WHEN 'deposit' THEN +txn_amount WHEN 'withdrawal' THEN -txn_amount END AS signed_amount  
• Recursive calendar CTE between min(txn_date) and max(txn_date) → produces “all months” so that customers with no activity still appear with prior balance carried forward  

Exploratory SQL queries  
The following 10 queries (LIMIT 20) move from simple inspection to a full closing‑balance prototype.  
